Let $l\ge8$. Suppose that the ordinary derivatives of $z$ through order $l$ have uniform $L^2$ bounds on images of compact rectangles in the lower cap, and that the metric satisfies the hypothesis of [prop:cap](#prop:cap). Then $u=\partial_y^l z$, re-expressed in flow coordinates, satisfies $$\label{eq:linear-cap}
u_{tt}+Au_{ss}+Bu_t+Cu_s=R_l,$$ where $R_l$ is uniformly bounded in $L^2$ on smaller compact rectangles, and $$\label{eq:linear-coefficients}
\begin{gathered}
A=G_1K,\qquad G_1=Gs_y^2,\qquad
B=-P_{z_x}-2lq_y,\\
C=(l+1)A_s+O_l(A).
\end{gathered}$$ The function $G_1$ has positive lower and upper bounds and bounded first derivatives. The coefficients $A,A_t,A_s,B,B_s,C$ are uniformly bounded.

Retain the model geometry and flow coordinates fixed above. Let $l\ge8$, and let the coefficients satisfy <a href="#eq:linear-coefficients" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:linear-coefficients">[eq:linear-coefficients]</a> with the uniform bounds in [lem:high-equation](#lem:high-equation). For every $R_0\Subset(-2,2)\times(-2,b_*)$, there is a larger compact rectangle $R_1$ in that cap and a constant $C_{R_0,l}$ such that every smooth solution of $$u_{tt}+Au_{ss}+Bu_t+Cu_s=f$$ on a neighborhood of $R_1$ satisfies $$\label{eq:gradient-bound}
\left\lVert(u_t,u_s)\right\rVert_{L^2(R_0)}
\le C_{R_0,l}\bigl(\left\lVert u\right\rVert_{L^2(R_1)}+\left\lVert f\right\rVert_{L^2(R_1)}\bigr).$$ The constants are uniform over the families under consideration.
